// `#when <condition> ... #end` gates a whole block, where `#in <state>+` gates
// on the state machine. A second word rather than a second meaning for `#in`:
// `#in Idle` reads as "in this state", and one word with two senses makes both
// harder to read.
//
// It compiles to the condition plus ONE OP_NINSTATE against zero -- the opcode
// `#in` already uses, with a different immediate -- so no new opcode and no ROM
// format change.
#digital Drdy in falling 2:13
#variable Ticks = 0
#variable A = 0
#variable B = 0
#variable Seen = 0

// Runs every cycle, so it wakes the block's rules reactively whether or not the
// gate holds. That is the property under test: a rule in the block must not run
// because its OWN dependency changed.
Ticks = Ticks + 1

#when Drdy.fired
  A = A + 1
  B = B + 1
  Seen = Ticks
#end
